+| R14 | Usage: every served call's `Decision` carries the provider-reported usage (input, output, cache reads, cache writes), streamed or not and whether or not the guest asked for it: OpenAI streams always request `include_usage` (the usage-only chunk is dropped again if the guest did not ask), and Anthropic usage is read from `message_start` and `message_delta`. Output is capped: every call goes upstream with `max_tokens`/`max_completion_tokens` at or below the owner's ceiling (`MaxOutputTokens`, default 32,000), so the OP-8 meter can reserve input plus that ceiling before the call. Arbitrator ruling: reported usage on a complete response is authoritative; when `Reported` is false or `Complete` is false (a cut-off stream), the meter falls back to `OutputChars` (content and tool-argument characters the provider produced), which is also the floor for a cut-off stream. The router hands each served call's usage to its caller through the request context (`WithUsage`); the meter settles from it (P1-7). Usage is `Reported` only when the provider gave an output count (`output_tokens`, `completion_tokens`); a usage object without one would charge no output, so the meter counts content instead. An Anthropic stream is `Complete` only when it reached `message_stop` and `message_delta` reported the output count. A provider answer the router cannot use (unreadable, too large, untranslatable) is reported with its size as `OutputChars`, since it may still be billed. `n` other than 1 never reaches the router: the meter in front of it refuses it. | OP-8 (v0.12), CAP-9 | Tune the default with the budget re-estimate. |
